       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like it might be a mistake.\n\n**The problem:**\n- **Each dose:** 1600 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of ibuprofen (800 mg).\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times a day comes to **6400 mg/day**, twice the usual prescription maximum of 3200 mg/day for adults.\n- **Risk:** Doses this high raise the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and other toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**Did you mean one of these?**\n1. **400 mg by mouth four times daily** (1600 mg/day total). This is common if \"1600\" was meant as the daily total.\n2. **800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3200 mg/day, the maximum).\n3. **600 mg by mouth four times daily** (2400 mg/day).\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, for example under a specific protocol, tell me and I'll enter it with a note saying you confirmed the dose and why. Otherwise, give me the correct dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
